# static-site workflow

## Commits

- Commit in meaningful units. Messages should state **what** changed and **why**.

## Linear

- Track work in **Linear** when your team uses it.
- Use the **Linear** MCP tools when available.

## reply-bridge (copy & facts)

- When changing product copy, FAQ, legal, or ads text, check **`/Users/hojin/Work/tldr/reply-bridge`** `marketing/` and `docs/` first.
- If the two repos disagree, **align static-site to reply-bridge**, not the reverse.
- Do not put absolute filesystem paths in built site content—those references are for agents and contributors only.

## Docs

- Summary, commands, directory map: `docs/AGENT.md`.

## Scope

- Changes belong in VitePress **`docs/`**, **`.vitepress`**, workflows, and static assets. Do not edit reply-bridge Go/iOS code in this repo.
